        <div data-pjax="true" data-test-selector="body-content" data-view-component="true" class="markdown-body tmp-my-3"><p>Daedalus 6.0.1 is a mainnet release upgrading to node <a href="https://github.com/IntersectMBO/cardano-node/releases/tag/9.1.1">9.1.1</a> to fix the ledger replay issue in the Conway era reported <a href="https://discord.com/channels/826816523368005654/862918105835110400/1279955818669674537" rel="nofollow">here</a>.<br>
This release prevents nodes replaying from genesis, and instead replay as normal. It is mandatory for all Daedalus users to upgrade to this version.</p>
<p>If you have already experienced this issue, your Daedalus will likely replay the ledger state from genesis (0%), so you may see longer synchronization times.</p>
<p>Please read the <a href="https://iohk.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/37188014124697" rel="nofollow">release notes</a> for more information.</p>
<p>Download Daedalus for Mainnet at <a href="https://daedaluswallet.io/en/download/?utm_source=github&amp;utm_medium=github&amp;utm_campaign=github" rel="nofollow">daedaluswallet.io</a>.</p>
<p>Download Daedalus for Preview and Pre-prod testnets at <a href="https://docs.cardano.org/cardano-testnets/tools/daedalus-testnet/?utm_source=github&amp;utm_medium=github&amp;utm_campaign=github" rel="nofollow">docs.cardano.org</a>.</p>
<h2>Installer integrity verification</h2>
<h3>PGP signatures</h3>
<p>Installers are signed with IOHK's organisational PGP key with this fingerprint: <code>53D0 FA8D A2B8 D1FF 4975 AECB F99D 6C70 C2B3 FB43</code>.<br>
<a href="https://keys.openpgp.org/vks/v1/by-fingerprint/53D0FA8DA2B8D1FF4975AECBF99D6C70C2B3FB43" rel="nofollow">https://keys.openpgp.org/vks/v1/by-fingerprint/53D0FA8DA2B8D1FF4975AECBF99D6C70C2B3FB43</a></p></div>
</div>
